     "hex": "0cdd10069f115402030000cc10041b032f83000200000000a70754020304ac200b012f830002000000000b002004a70754000300ac2019032ec1a2b04202000429012ec1a2b0420200083c80233e0000000c40604b00260040000010000057265402004049005746540420404a0057165400404048005786540660404b005706550880404c000e000000",
     "len": 138
    }
   },
   "why": "Direct replication of EXP-0162's `pixel_order` carrier (same src, clear, reset, instance count), so its committed per-value partition is a PRE-REGISTERED PREDICTION this run is scored against rather than an inert 'differs from baseline' oracle. Ordering failure presents as a LOST-UPDATE COUNT; being commutative, this carrier is blind to a pure permutation."
  },
